    {
      "dom_id": "question-317613",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "A video was posted on a streaming platform with $50$ initial views. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each hour after the video was posted, the number of views increased by $120%$ of the number of views at the end of the previous hour.\n\nAccording to this model, how many views are there estimated to be after $3$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of views $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $120%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=50$ is the total number of views initially\n\n- $r=1.2$ is the growth rate ($120%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours) after the video was posted\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=50\\cdot (1+1.2)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=50\\cdot (2.2)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of views after $3$ hours, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=50\\cdot (2.2)^{3}≈532\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of views after $3$ hours is $532.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-317613\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">3.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/2471#21183\">Modeling Exponential Growth Using Percentage Increases Greater Than 100%</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"317613\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>A video was posted on a streaming platform with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"37\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> initial views. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each hour after the video was posted, the number of views increased by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"38\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c25\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> of the number of views at the end of the previous hour.</p>\n<p>According to this model, how many views are there estimated to be after <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"39\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c cl