    {
      "dom_id": "question-318202",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "When a new article was first published on a news website, it had $40$ views. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each hour after publication, the number of views increased by $190%$ of the number of views at the end of the previous hour.\n\nWhich of the following equations best represents this model, where $V$ is the estimated number of views $t$ hours after the article was published, and $t\\le 6?$",
      "worked_solution": "The number of views $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $190%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=40$ is the total number of views initially\n\n- $r=1.9$ is the growth rate ($190%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours) after publication\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=40\\cdot (1+1.9)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=40\\cdot (2.9)^{t}.\n$$",
